#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Resources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kaddressbook; can use multiple resources for loading and storing its contacts. "
"After starting &kaddressbook; for the first time you will have a default "
"resource installed that saves all contacts in a vCard file under "
"$HOME/.kde/share/apps/kabc/std.vcf; you can add more resources by using the "
"Resource Configuration dialog, which is available in <application>"
"kcontrol</application> under <guilabel>KDE Components</guilabel>-><guilabel>"
"KDE Resources Configuration</guilabel>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Resource Configuration Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Resource Configuration Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Resource Configuration Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Load the configuration module you want to add your resource(s) to. By selecting "
"it from the combo box at the top of the <guilabel>Resources</guilabel> "
"section. The module for &kaddressbook; being <guilabel>contact</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Launch the <guilabel>Resource Configuration</guilabel> "
"dialog by pushing the <guibutton>Add...</guibutton> button. Choose the resource "
"you want to add to your <guilabel>contact</guilabel> module and click <guilabel>"
"OK</guilabel> to confirm your choice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directory"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "each contact will be stored in its own file;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "File"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "all contacts will be stored in one file;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "IMAP"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143 index.docbook:164 index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "To be written"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kolab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "The contacts will be saved in the contact folder of your DIMAP account."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Kolab server specificities:</guilabel> The Kolab resource should "
"never be configured as Read Only. In case you have added several types of "
"resources you need to set your <guilabel>Kolab Server</guilabel> "
"resource as your <guilabel>Standard</guilabel> resource."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "LDAP"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "all contacts will be stored on a LDAP server;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Network"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"all contacts will be stored in one file, which can be located on a remote "
"server (for example, through HTTP, WebDAV, FTP or Fish)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "SLOX"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After selecting the type of resource another dialog appears where you can "
"configure the resource-specific settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>File</guilabel> and <guilabel>Directory</guilabel> "
"resource supports different formats for storing the contacts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:180 index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid "vCard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the contacts will be stored in the vCard format, as specified in RFC 2426;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "binary"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the contacts will be stored in a binary format &mdash; this increases "
"performance during loading and saving, but it is not portable like the vCard "
"format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kaddressbook; needs a standard resource, where all contacts should be saved if "
"no other resource is specified; for this reason, after starting &kaddressbook; "
"the first time, there is already a resource available. If you want to use "
"another resource as the standard resource, use the <guibutton>"
"Use as Standard</guibutton> button to select it. You must have both read and "
"write access to the new standard resource, otherwise you won't be able to "
"select it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing Contacts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create or edit contacts, &kaddressbook; offers a dialog where you can input "
"all the data that can be stored in a vCard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Contact Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Contact Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Contact Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Name Parsing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kaddressbook; tries to provide an easy name input by automatic name parsing; "
"for this to work properly it is sometimes necessary to add custom name "
"prefixes, suffixes or inclusions in the <link "
"linkend=\"preferences-address-book-contact\">configure dialog</link>"
". Nevertheless, no algorithm is perfect, so the name you enter may be parsed "
"incorrectly; in this case, you can disable the automatic name parsing in the "
"name edit dialog, which is available by clicking the <guibutton>"
"Name...</guibutton> button in the contact dialog. If you wish to disable the "
"name parsing for all new contacts you can disable automatic name parsing "
"globally in the <link linkend=\"preferences-address-book-general\">"
"configure dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatted Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The formatted name of a contact is used by other programs to represent it. "
"&kaddressbook; offers three predefined types of formatted names:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "SimpleName"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;given name&gt; &lt;family name&gt;;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "FullName"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;prefix&gt; &lt;given name&gt; &lt;additional name&gt; &lt;family name&gt; "
"&lt;suffix&gt;;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "ReverseName"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;family name&gt;, &lt;given name&gt;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If none of the above types fit your needs you can select the <guilabel>"
"Custom</guilabel> name type, where you can add your own formatted name &mdash; "
"this configuration can be done in the name edit dialog. To specify a default "
"formatted name type for new contacts, use the <link "
"linkend=\"preferences-address-book-contact\">configure dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "Instant Messaging"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>IM Address</guilabel> text box holds the preferred Instant "
"Messaging Address for this contact. To add, view and edit additional IM "
"Addresses, click the <guilabel>Edit IM Addresses...</guilabel> "
"button. The Edit IM Addresses Dialog appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Edit IM Addresses Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Edit IM Addresses Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Edit IM Addresses Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A contact can have multiple instant messaging addresses associated with it. "
"Other applications, such as <application>Kopete</application> and <application>"
"Konversation</application>, store their information here. It is recommended "
"that you add, edit and delete instant messaging addresses in <application>"
"Kopete</application> or <application>Konversation</application> "
"rather than here, since they can assist you better in adding the address, "
"adding the user to a group, and so on. If you are not interested in whether "
"they are picked up in another application, and just want to store the instant "
"messaging address with the contact, then it is fine to add and edit it here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on adding new Instant Messaging Addresses, see <ulink "
"url=\"help:/kopete/getting-started.html#creating-accounts\"><application>"
"Kopete</application>'s handbook</ulink> and <ulink "
"url=\"help:/konversation/linkaddressbook.html\"><application>"
"Konversation</application>'s handbook</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "Crypto Settings tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this tab, you can define preferences with regards to cryptography for a "
"contact. At the time of this writing, only <application>KMail</application> "
"will make use of these preferences when composing messages. This mechanism "
"replaces the barely editable per-recipient crypto preferences of earlier "
"<application>KMail</application> releases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allowed Protocols"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, you can restrict the cryptographic message formats that can be used for "
"this contact. See the section on <ulink "
"url=\"/kmail/the-composer-window.html#cryptographic-message-formats\">"
"Cryptographic Message Formats</ulink> in <ulink url=\"/kmail/\"><application>"
"KMail</application>'s handbook</ulink> for a discussion of the different "
"available formats."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Preferred OpenPGP encryption key</guilabel>, <guilabel>"
"Preferred S/MIME encryption certificate</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, you can assign a preferred OpenPGP key and/or S/MIME certificate to be "
"used when encrypting to this contact. Otherwise, the local keyring and local "
"certificate box are searched for matching keys and certificates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Message Preference"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, you can select from a set of directives for user interaction both when "
"signing and when encrypting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;none&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No preference, use whatever mode <application>KMail</application> defaults to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Never Sign</guilabel>, <guilabel>Never Encrypt</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Never sign (encrypt) messages to this contact. Don't ask for confirmation "
"(except in the case of conflicts with preferences of other contacts)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Always Sign</guilabel>, <guilabel>Always Encrypt</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Always sign (encrypt) messages to the contact. Don't ask for confirmation "
"(except in the case of conflicts with preferences of other contacts)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Always Sign If Possible</guilabel>, <guilabel>"
"Always Encrypt If Possible</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Always sign (encrypt) messages to this contact when it would be possible to do "
"so. Don't ask if it isn't possible. Situations in which signing might not be "
"possible include other recipients having signing preferences of \"Never\". "
"Situations in which encryption might not be possible include missing "
"keys/certificates for this or other recievers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Ask</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always ask whether to sign (encrypt)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Views"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this version, &kaddressbook; offers different views, which can represent the "
"contacts in different ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid "Table View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All contacts are listed in a table; they can be sorted by clicking at the "
"column header of the table. The columns of the table depend on the fields which "
"were selected in the view configuration dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icon View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The contacts are listed as icons in a view. If the contact contains a photo or "
"logo, then it is used in the view; otherwise, an default icon is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid "Card View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All contacts are presented in form of cards. The titles of these cards are the "
"formatted names; the body of each card depends on what fields were selected in "
"the view configuration dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid "The View Configuration Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The View Configuration Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The View Configuration Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Selected Fields</guilabel> page offers you the possibility of "
"selecting which of the stored details of a contact should be shown in the view. "
"In the <guilabel>Default Filter</guilabel> page you can setup what <link "
"linkend=\"using-filters\">filter</link> should be used by the view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can setup filters in &kaddressbook; which depend on the categories a "
"contact belongs to. For example, you can create a filter that matches all "
"contacts which belong to the categories 'Family' and 'Friends'; you can also "
"create a filter that matches all contacts which do not these categories. To "
"manage filters, use the filter configuration dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Filter Configuration Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Filter Configuration Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Filter Configuration Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Filters can be used in views to reduce the number of contacts shown. In the "
"<link linkend=\"using-filters\">view configuration dialog</link> "
"you can specify what filter should be used by a view by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Extensions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Extensions are implemented as plugins in &kaddressbook;, so 3rd-party "
"developers can provide more of them. At the moment we already have three "
"extensions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contact Editor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Similar to the the contact editing dialog, but designed to allow contacts to be "
"edited quickly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "Location of Contact"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This extension takes the postal address of a contact and loads a map service "
"from the internet (like www.map24.de) with these data; the result is shown in a "
"<acronym>HTML</acronym> view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "Distribution List Manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This extension provides easy management of the distribution lists: just create "
"a new list and select a contact in the view; then, after clicking <guibutton>"
"Add contact</guibutton>, the selected contact is part of the distribution list. "
"A simpler way is to drag a contact from the view and drop it over the "
"distribution list manager. See <link linkend=\"settings-menu\"> "
"Settings Menu</link> about how to add an extension."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The main window with distribution list extension.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:525
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The main window with distribution list extension.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The main window with distribution list extension.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid "Import and Export"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the new import/export framework &kaddressbook; offers a dialog where you "
"can select which contacts are to be exported."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The export selection dialog.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The export selection dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The export selection dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following import and export plugins are available at the moment:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the vCard format is standardized format (RFC 2426) that is supported by most "
"addressbook applications &mdash; &kaddressbook; can import and export versions "
"2.1 and 3.0;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mobile Phone"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this plugin can import contacts from Nokia mobile phones via the gnokii "
"library;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid "Eudora Addressbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
